5. Ethanethiolate: weaker base than hydroxide (pKa of ethanethiol ~10)

So, the basicity order from strongest to weakest is: 1 > 2 > 5 > 3 > 4.

If nucleophilicity in polar protic solvents is inversely related to basicity, then the nucleophilicity order would be: 3 (propionate) < 5 (ethanethiolate) < 2 (hydroxide) < 1 (alkoxide) < 4 (methanol). Wait, no. If weaker bases are better nucleophiles, then the order would be: 3 (propionate) < 5 (ethanethiolate) < 2 (hydroxide) < 1 (alkoxide) < 4 (methanol)? No, that doesn't make sense. Let me think again.

