gpqa,"You are studying the patterns of inheritance between genes A and B on the same chromosome. They are on the same autosome and about 50 centimorgans apart. You believe they are linked, but you are not sure. The gene A codes for tail length so that the A1 allele is homozygous recessive and produces a long tail. The allele A2 is the dominant allele and codes for a short tail. The gene B codes for ear size; B1 is small, and B2 is large. Both of the B alleles are co-dominant. One parent of your F1 generation has A1B2/A1B2 genotype and long tail and large ears phenotype. The other parent is short-tailed with medium-sized ears and has the A1B1/A2B2 genotype. Unexpectedly, you find that all of their offspring are short-tailed. What is the relationship among the alleles?","[""allele A2 is imprinted"", ""B1 allele modifies A1 homozygotes"", ""allele A1 is not the recessive allele"", ""the genes A and B are not linked""]",B,"Okay, let's try to figure this out. So the question is about gene linkage between A and B, which are 50 centimorgans apart. The parents are A1B2/A1B2 (long tail, large ears) and A1B1/A2B2 (short tail, medium ears). All the offspring are short-tailed. The options are about imprinting, modification, recessiveness, or linkage.

