Number of half-lives n = t / T_total = 600 / 5.698 ≈ 105.27. So the remaining fraction is (1/2)^105.27. Which is an extremely small number. Let's see, (1/2)^10 = 1/1024 ≈ 1e-3, (1/2)^100 ≈ (1e-3)^10 = 1e-30, so (1/2)^105 is about 1e-30 * (1/2)^5 ≈ 1e-30 * 1/32 ≈ 3e-32. So N(t) ≈ 5e34 * 3e-32 ≈ 1.5e3 = 1500. Then, A_alpha = λ_alpha * N(t) ≈ 0.00385 * 1500 ≈ 5.775 Bq. Hmm, but this is different from the previous 3.85 Bq. Wait, why the discrepancy?

