Then, [Co(SCN)₂⁺] is 40 * 0.00423 * 0.01 (since [SCN⁻]^2 is 0.01). Wait, let me recheck that calculation.

[Co(SCN)₂⁺] = β2 * x * [SCN⁻]^2 = 40 * 0.00423 * (0.1)^2.

(0.1)^2 is 0.01. So 40 * 0.00423 * 0.01 = 40 * 0.0000423 = 0.001692. Yes, that's correct.

So 0.001692 / 0.01 = 0.1692, so 16.92%, which rounds to 16.9%, so option B.

