But let me check if there's another possible interpretation. For example, maybe the blue complex is [Co(SCN)₄]²⁻, but that's not dithiocyanato. Dithiocyanato is di-thio-cyanato, so two SCN⁻ ligands. So yes, [Co(SCN)₂]⁺ is the correct one. Therefore, the percentage is 16.9%, which is option B.

However, I need to check if the question is asking for the percentage of all dithiocyanato complexes, but since there's only one complex with two SCN⁻ ligands, which is [Co(SCN)₂]⁺, then our calculation is correct.

