Therefore, the only change is the ketone to CH2, adding one. 

Thus, the answer is B) 7.",ANSWER: B
gpqa,"Let a pendulum consist of an object hanging from a support, such that its lagrangian is given by 1/2*M*R*R*theta-dot*theta-dot - 4/3*M*g*R*(1-cos(theta)). The pendulum is released from rest, at an initial angle alpha. An expression for the period of the pendulum is given by the integral of which integrand? (In the previous expression, theta-dot represents the time derivative of the angle between pendulum and vertical, theta). ","[""sqrt(3*R/(8*g)) / sqrt((sin(alpha) - cos(theta)))"", ""sqrt(3*R/(8*g)) / sqrt((cos(theta) \u2013 cos(alpha)))"", ""sqrt(6*R/g) / sqrt((cos(theta) - cos(alpha)))"", ""sqrt(6*R/g) / sqrt((sin(alpha) \u2013 cos(theta)))""]",C,"Okay, let's see. I need to figure out the period of a pendulum based on the given Lagrangian. The question is asking which integral expression gives the period. The options are A, B, C, D.

