But the period is the time to go from θ = α down to -α and back to α. However, since the pendulum is released from rest at θ=α, the period is four times the time to go from θ=α to θ=0 (because it goes from α to 0, then 0 to -α, then -α to 0, then 0 to α). Wait, actually, the period is the time for a full cycle. So, if we consider the motion from θ=α to θ=-α and back, but integrating over half the period might be easier.

