But the integral is ∫ [dθ / sqrt(cosθ - cosα) ] multiplied by sqrt(6R/g). So the period is the integral from θ=α to θ=-α (but split into four parts) of the same expression. However, the question is asking for the integrand of the integral that gives the period. So the period is expressed as the integral of (sqrt(6R/g) / sqrt(cosθ - cosα)) dθ over some interval.

