ait, the absorption line in this case is observed in the Milky Way. Wait, but the question says observations of structures at 2.1 Gpc, which is a distance of about 6.8 billion light years. That's outside the Milky Way. But the question is asking what is most likely to be observed with this absorption line in the Milky Way. Wait, maybe the absorption line is from the Milky Way's ISM. Wait, the question is a bit confusing. Let me re-read.

