hle,"The endohedral fullerene Ce2@C80 is reacted with 1,1,2,2-tetrakis(2,4,6-trimethylphenyl)-1,2-disilirane. What is the effect on the cerium atoms?","[""The disilirane coordinates to the cerium atoms creating a M2L12 complex"", ""The disilirane coordinates to a cerium atom creating a ML6 complex"", ""The cerium atoms continue free random motion inside the fullerene"", ""The cerium atoms are now positioned at the equator of the fullerene"", ""The cerium atoms are now positioned at the poles of the fullerene""]",D,"Okay, so I need to figure out what happens to the cerium atoms when Ce2@C80 reacts with this disilirane compound. Let me start by recalling what endohedral fullerenes are. They're fullerenes with atoms or molecules trapped inside the carbon cage. In this case, there are two cerium atoms inside the C80 fullerene.

