F) Higher green densities leading to lower sintered densities. Green density is the density before sintering. If the green density is higher, maybe the material is more compact. But during sintering, if there's a coarsening gas, maybe the higher initial density leads to less densification, but that seems counterintuitive. Or perhaps the gas causes defects that reduce the final density despite higher green density. Not sure.

