So if semantic transparency is about the morphological structure being predictable, then languages with more inflection might be more transparent. So maybe Old English, being more inflected, is more transparent than Modern English. Similarly, German and Russian, being more inflected than Modern English, might have higher transparency. But how do German and Russian compare? Russian is a Slavic language with a complex case system, while German has cases too but maybe fewer than Russian? I'm not sure.

