But I'm not certain. Given the options, and my uncertainty, but considering that Old English is more transparent than Modern English, and German and Russian are more than Modern English, but I can't decide between German and Russian. If I have to choose between C and D, and C has Modern English higher than German and Russian, which I think is incorrect, while D has Russian > German > Old English. But I'm not sure about Old English vs German and Russian. Maybe Old English is less transparent than German and Russian because German and Russian have more complex systems. If that's the case, then the order could be Russian > German > Old English > Modern English (option D). But I'm not sure.

Alternatively, maybe the correct answer is C: Old English > Modern English > German > Russian. But why would Modern English be more transparent than German and Russian? That seems unlikely.

Hmm. This is tricky. I think I need to make an educated guess. Given that Old English is more transparent than Modern English, and German and Russian are more transparent than Modern English, and assuming that between German and Russian, Russian is more transparent (due to more cases), then the order would be Old English > Russian > German > Modern English, which isn't an option. However, option D is Russian > German > Old English > Modern English. If that's the case, then Old English is more transparent than Modern English but less than German and Russian. But I'm not sure. Alternatively, if Müller-Gotama's theory says that German is more transparent than Russian, then maybe the order is Old English > German > Russian > Modern English, but again, not an option.

