Standard sign conventions for mirrors: Object distance (do) is positive if the object is in front of the mirror (real object). For convex mirrors, the focal length (f) is negative because the focal point is behind the mirror. The radius of curvature (R) is related to f by f = R/2. So if the mirror is convex, R is negative because the center of curvature is behind the mirror. Therefore, f = R/2 would be negative.

