Alternatively, the basic intrinsic good might be the ultimate end, which is God, but the question is about basic intrinsic goods that are part of natural law. The primary precepts are the basic goods that are ordered towards the ultimate end. So maybe all three options are considered primary precepts. If that's the case, then D) all of the above would be correct.

