So the key point is that when BCAAs are deaminated in muscle, the ammonia is converted into non-toxic compounds like alanine and glutamine. Then these are released into the bloodstream. The liver can then process the ammonia from these amino acids. So the answer would be D: converted into alanine and glutamine and released from the muscle.",ANSWER: D
