mmlu_pro,"Adams Manufacturing Company recently suffered a fire loss of $45,000. Their insurance was distributed between two insurance companies as follows: Company Name Amount of Policy Acme Insurance $50,000 Safe Way Insurance $30,000 How much of the loss did each of the insurance companies pay to Adams?","[""Acme Insurance - $25,000, Safe Way Insurance - $20,000"", ""Acme Insurance - $22,500, Safe Way Insurance - $22,500"", ""Acme Insurance - $20,000, Safe Way Insurance - $25,000"", ""Acme Insurance - $28,125, Safe Way Insurance - $16,875"", ""Acme Insurance - $26,250, Safe Way Insurance - $18,750"", ""Acme Insurance - $33,750, Safe Way Insurance - $11,250"", ""Acme Insurance - $27,000, Safe Way Insurance - $18,000"", ""Acme Insurance - $30,000, Safe Way Insurance - $15,000"", ""Acme Insurance - $32,500, Safe Way Insurance - $12,500"", ""Acme Insurance - $24,000, Safe Way Insurance - $21,000""]",D,"Okay, let's see. Adams Manufacturing had a fire loss of $45,000. They have two insurance companies: Acme with a $50,000 policy and Safe Way with $30,000. The question is how much each company pays.

