Using logarithm tables or approximation. The difference between 4 and 4.3 is 0.3. The derivative of log(x) is 1/(x ln10). At x=4, derivative is 1/(4 * 2.3026) ≈ 1/9.21 ≈ 0.1086 per unit x. So for an increase of 0.3 in x from 4 to 4.3, the approximate increase in log(x) is 0.3 * 0.1086 ≈ 0.0326. Therefore, log(4.3) ≈ log(4) + 0.0326 ≈ 0.60206 + 0.0326 ≈ 0.6347. Therefore, pKa = -log(4.3 × 10^-7) = 7 - 0.6347 = 6.3653. So pKa ≈ 6.365.

Then, pH - pKa = 7.40 - 6.365 = 1.035.

