Back to A and B. Inflation (A) would cause all prices to rise, so even if the farmer's price drops, other costs might go up, leading to higher retail prices. B is about retailers increasing profit margins. If the farmer's price is lower, but the retailer keeps the same markup, the retail price would decrease. But if they increase their margin, then the retail price could rise even if the farmer's price is lower. So B is possible. But why would they do that? Maybe if they have market power. However, in a competitive market, they might not be able to. 

